------------------------------------------------------------------------
CODE SHARED WITH SATOM
------------------------------------------------------------------------
The installer and the update system (installers/, deploy/) reuse code
from SATOM, the sister product by the same licensor, under the same
license. Every vendored file and function is listed, with its source
path and the SATOM revision it was taken from, in deploy/VENDORED.md.
Nothing is imported from SATOM at runtime.

------------------------------------------------------------------------
THIRD-PARTY COMPONENTS
------------------------------------------------------------------------
Python dependencies are declared in requirements.txt and, for offline
installs and update packages, staged as wheels inside the bundle or the
package. They are not modified; each retains the license published by
its author. Operating-system packages staged in an offline bundle
(.deb / .rpm) are unmodified copies of the distribution's own artefacts
and remain under the distribution's terms.

